From 505f4f5edf6b12b7a51b9aba137851bc5194648d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 19:55:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: dedicated Addons section - lift every addon contribution
 out of the stock menus

Field: Merlin addons rearranged the left rail, swapped icons and turned a stock
menu into a flat addon list; removing the addon put the rail back.

Cause: ReaperAddons.isAddonMenu() classed a whole menu as an addon menu the
moment one user<N>.asp tab landed in it (YazFi into Wireless), and addon menus
pushed mid-list (or under an index of their own) rendered wherever they sat.

Now ReaperAddons.split() is the single rule for both rails: addon menus are
dropped, addon tabs are stripped out of stock menus (shallow copies; the live
menuTree is never mutated), and every entry collects in ONE dedicated section
at the end of the rail - a single "Addons" item with a count that unfolds the
list (auto-open when an addon page is active). The shell tab bar for an addon
page is the addon set; stock tab bars no longer carry addon tabs. Nothing is
emitted when no addon is installed. Dashboard rail mirrors it via the text-mode
fromText() twin. New dict key Reaper_c_addons in all 25 packs (6768 lockstep).

Mock-verified against three injection styles (menu_Addons block mid-list,
user<N>.asp tab inside Wireless, foreign menu_Diversion menu): 0 JS errors.
